        "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
        "revision": 1315245508,
        "heading": "Uses",
        "text": "Resin was traditionally used as a washing agent in Arabia.  The hardened resin was mixed with water or spittle and then rubbed over the body.  It was also a treatment to treat head lice.  It is an important fodder and the wood was used to make fishing platforms.",
